From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:58:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] deps: Bump mozjs to 0.26.14

Upstream moved mozjs to 0.26.13 with its off-thread compilation of
classic scripts (#45687), and to 0.26.14 for a potential out-of-bounds
read (#49514). Take 0.26.14 on ohos-main ahead of the next sync, so
that the QuickJS shim, which follows ohos-main's mozjs version, can
move to it and be tested on its own. ohos-main needs no code change
for it: what the newer mozjs adds is the API of the off-thread
compilation, which ohos-main doesn't use yet.

Keep it until the base requires 0.26.14 itself. Servo 0.8.0 requires
0.26.13; upstream's bump to 0.26.14 (bbad078a6c2) came after it and,
like this commit, changes only the version.

Validation: `cargo update -p mozjs` changes only the mozjs crates (mozjs 0.26.14, mozjs_sys 153.6.0-2 and its ICU and glue crates 153.6.0); a release build with SpiderMonkey passes, and `./mach test-wpt --release html/webappapis/scripting/events` runs its 51 tests as expected. The SpiderMonkey tests whose results on this host differ from ohos-main's stored CI run give the same results with ohos-main before this commit, three runs each (image-percentage-height, stale-while-revalidate's stale-css, -image and -script, element_click/navigate.py, window-open-multi-global, which timed out 3 of 3 times before and 2 of 3 after).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent during the 2026-11-08 sync)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
